# Secrets. Never commit — this repo is public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The source resume: a personal document carrying a phone number and address.
# Rooted at this repo's root, which IS steve/portfolio — do not prefix the path.
#
# The *published* copy is a separate, deliberate choice: slice 07 puts a resume
# at site/public/resume.pdf, which is tracked and served. This rule covers the
# working document sitting beside the plans, not that one.
/Stephen_Ade_O_Resume.pdf

# Build output and dependencies. site/ carries its own .gitignore too; these
# are the root-level backstop so a stray install at the wrong depth cannot be
# committed by a `git add -A`.
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.output/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Terraform. State carries account ids and resource ARNs; .terraform/ carries
# provider binaries measured in hundreds of megabytes.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log

# Local editor and tool state.
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local state. settings.json IS tracked — it is the shared wiring.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/session-log.md
.claude/worktrees/

# Tool scratch output.
.playwright-mcp/
.lighthouseci/

# Session handoffs are working notes, not project history.
/HANDOFF.md

# Build planning documents. Deliberately untracked: they describe how the repo
# is being built rather than forming part of the shipped project, and they name
# a reference implementation and an owner's private resume. They live on disk
# for whoever is running the build — see docs/plans/README.md — and are backed
# up outside the repo, not recovered from git.
/docs/
